WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.910
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.640
<i>The major event that rocked
the imperial capital has ended,</i>

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.350
<i>ushering in a brief respite.</i>

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:11.360
<i>The girl returns home to her 
waiting brother Hitaki,</i>

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.630
<i>along with Nabari Yutaka, who was 
once a student houseboy in their home.</i>

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.260
<i>As they enter the Kuze family library,</i>

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.700
<i>where Hitaki found the cursed tome,</i>

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.630
<i>a sinister gleam appears in Nabari's eyes.</i>

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.760
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her conclusion.</i>

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.070
<i>Libra of Nil Admirari.</i>

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.580
Nabari-san?

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.310
So... when you said you saw auras in here...

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.580
Yes, it was a lie.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.650
Huh?

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.530
I knew you both would readily believe me.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.150
What do you mean? Why would you lie?

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:52.830
As I said, I wanted it to 
be just the three of us.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.000
Do you remember the first time we met?

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.600
When I arrived at your home 
as a student houseboy...

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.420
You both welcomed me, a complete stranger,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.850
with such sincere smiles.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:17.430
Right away, you idolized me 
as if I were your older brother.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:17.430
Here you go.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:18.350
Thank you.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.360
Your smiles

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.130
allowed me to dream of a 
happy time that was long gone.

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.750
Nabari-san...

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.530
I don't have a home.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:37.360
When I was a child, I lived happily with my 
mother and father. Just the three of us.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:39.370
But...

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.020
My father was conscripted to be a soldier,

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.890
and died in action.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:01.110
Even when the war ended, 
my father never came home.

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:06.200
I'd never see him—never 
hear his voice—ever again!

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.400
Mama, don't cry.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:12.090
Don't cry. I'm here.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:12.880
Darling...

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.050
I'll protect you, Mama.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:19.370
Darling, why? Darling!

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:22.920
<i>And then, one day...</i>

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.420
I'm going to be with your father.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.420
Mama! Mama!

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.120
Mama!

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.700
Nabari-san, I'm so sorry...

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.210
My apologies for the wait.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.720
They all went to the library.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:53.450
The library?

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.450
Yes, they said there was something 
they wanted to look into.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:02:59.950
What could it be?

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.200
I've lost my father and 
mother, and have no home.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.840
But when I'm with the two of you, 
I feel like I can go back to it.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.850
To my home in the flames, 
to that place of eternal happiness.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.240
Mama...

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.860
Oh, Mama...

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.980
Tsugumi-sama?

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.480
It's locked?

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.120
When I thought about the home I lost,

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:38.550
the crackling flames in my 
heart would burst forth.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.260
The black smoke would whirl
thunderously around me.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:47.680
It was hot, painful, and so intense 
that I couldn't breathe...

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:54.270
I started writing books to drive 
those flames out of my heart.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:56.270
Books?

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:03.620
When I'm writing, the flames in my heart 
become ever so slightly calmer.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.090
When I finish writing, 
the pain becomes lighter,

00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:12.290
and I'm able to breathe a bit better.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:16.600
But not long after, the flames 
once again spiral out of control,

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.970
and they begin slowly burning 
my heart worse than before.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.880
So then, I write a book again.

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:26.440
And they're cursed tomes?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:31.440
That's right, Tsugumi-kun. 
Have a look for yourself. See?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.500
Nee-san?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.410
Nee-san!

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.480
Nee-san!

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.190
It's finished.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.070
My first book.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:06.210
<i>A flaming cursed tome.</i>

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:10.210
That's strange... These flames aren't hot.

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:15.930
I wonder if it can see 
the flames in my heart.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:16.880
Nabari-san!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:25.080
Welcome to the Imperial Library 
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.840
Our primary function is to search 
out items known as cursed tomes,

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.230
books that have an effect on 
the mind of their readers,

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:35.540
and deal with them appropriately.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.810
Light?

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.050
Lights are coming from the books...

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.250
Lights? So you can see the lights?!

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.420
Mashiko-san! Nabari-san!

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.270
Cursed tome...

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.300
The book I've written is a cursed tome?

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.270
What kind of effect would 
it have on a reader?

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.040
No!

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:19.550
Yasuhiko...

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.410
How terrible...

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:31.060
No... I must never write another book.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:38.060
No! No, no! Stop writing!

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:42.570
It hurts, it hurts... so hot...

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:48.100
I know. I'll change my name, 
and my handwriting.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:57.580
Where will you go? Who will read you?

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:00.950
My books, my books!

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:08.830
Hitaki!

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:17.410
No, no, no!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.510
No!

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.480
The marmalade you made was so delicious.

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:34.560
This beautiful marmalade 
with the color of the sun...

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:41.300
It reminds me of the strawberry 
jam my mama used to make.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.470
That is the taste of happiness.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:48.000
The taste of happiness, trapped inside a jar...

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:49.990
Mama.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:51.580
Mama.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.000
Mama.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.530
Mama...

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.560
Mama...

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.510
Relax. You're coming with us, too.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:11.520
Please open the door! 
Tsugumi-sama! Hitaki-sama!

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:15.670
Can you hear me?! Please 
open the door! Nabari-sama!

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.220
Is Kuze inside?!

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:22.370
Oh, Ozaki-sama! Yes, all 
three of them are in there.

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:27.560
Burning... Mama is burning...

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:30.950
She went away and left me behind.

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.770
My home is burning, too.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:36.780
Kuze!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.070
Hitaki-kun.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:40.780
I have to burn it all.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:46.050
Then I'll be able to go home and see Mama.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:51.060
I have to go back to the 
flames. I will go home.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:55.390
Burn it all, more and more...

00:09:07.220 --> 00:09:07.970
Kuze!

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.980
Kuze, get a hold of yourself!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.480
Kuze! Kuze!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.250
Get a hold of yourself!

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:19.750
Kuze!

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.250
Come on, Kuze!

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:26.220
Get a hold of yourself! 
Come to your senses! Kuze!

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:27.240
Hayato...

00:09:27.240 --> 00:09:28.790
Please, open your eyes!

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:32.280
Tsugumi!

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:44.010
Tsugumi!

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.510
Hayato?

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:52.020
Tsugumi... Thank God you're all right!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.520
Hayato...

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.140
Hitaki-sama!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:57.790
Gramps!

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:06.030
I'm sure you and Ozaki-kun 
both would like to kill me.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:07.530
Of course we would!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:13.540
You killed Yasuhiko!
I will <i>never</i> forgive you!

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.040
Kill me, then.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:19.950
I won't do that.

00:10:21.590 --> 00:10:25.170
A life lost cannot be paid 
for by another life.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.820
You must live and atone for your sins.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.330
Nabari-san.

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.930
I know you were incredibly sad.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:46.340
But the place you have to 
return to isn't in the flames.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:53.520
You have to find where you 
belong here in the real world.

00:10:55.200 --> 00:11:00.080
While you acknowledge and atone
for the crimes you've committed.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.900
So, what are your plans?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.050
You mean...

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.560
I mean, what are you going to do now?

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:45.820
Oh!

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.050
Hitaki-kun has been discharged,

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:50.210
so you have the option of going back home.

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:50.800
No.

00:11:51.320 --> 00:11:53.800
I'm going to stay here.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:57.240
I've found a place that's important to me,

00:11:57.240 --> 00:11:58.810
and I want to keep working here,

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.070
as a member of Fukurou.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.810
I love books.

00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:09.320
While a person's life might 
one day vanish, their heart

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:13.090
and feelings remain behind 
in the books they wrote.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:18.830
They may not be trying to convey 
something directly, like in cursed tomes.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:22.110
But thanks to books, we are able to learn

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:27.960
about the hearts of many people 
over many different time periods.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.640
Such as the love of a Heian girl,

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:33.210
or the sorrow of a king 
from Britain's Middle Ages.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:35.810
Yes, that's true.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.980
I want to keep protecting such books.

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:44.530
Is that so? I'm glad to hear 
that you'd like to stay.

00:12:44.530 --> 00:12:45.720
Don't you all agree?

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.020
P-Pardon us.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.220
You found us out, eh?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:54.640
Shougo? Shizuru-san?

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.860
So, um...

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.420
It's not like we were eavesdropping.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.230
We just happened to be in the library.

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.370
Right!

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:04.530
Yeah, that's it!

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:06.060
They apparently feel the same way.

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.900
Ukai-kun was the only one peeping.

00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:09.350
Wh-What?! How dare you?!

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:11.640
Besides, you were the one 
who said we should go!

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.450
Was I?

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.010
Am I wrong?

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:18.120
Isn't this great, Shiori?

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:19.620
Yes, it is.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:23.730
Excuse me, but in order for me to stay here,

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:26.690
there's something I need to take care of first.

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.550
Right through here.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.480
Thank you.

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.050
Pardon me.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.300
Nice to meet you. I'm Kuze Tsugumi.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:13.090
Please forgive me for my rudeness, but...

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:19.750
Huh?

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:25.060
Hey.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:26.700
H-Hayato?!

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.930
Wait, what are you doing here?

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.230
You can't just go sneaking into places.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.910
It's nice to meet you, Kuze Tsugumi-san.

00:14:38.910 --> 00:14:40.460
I am Yashiro Hayato.

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:43.330
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:47.840
Eh? Huh? Um...

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:51.340
I'm sorry I never told you.

00:14:51.770 --> 00:14:55.840
I'm the son of the president of the 
Yashiro Steamship, and your fiance.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:02.620
But your name is Ozaki Hayato... 
Your family name is Ozaki, right?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.780
Ozaki is a pseudonym.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.220
I wanted to work somewhere without 
the influence of my father's name.

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.400
Oh, I wasn't planning on trying to settle 
this whole marriage thing with money.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.870
For my part, I've known about 
you for quite some time,

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:24.520
and I've always thought that I'd 
like to spend my life with you.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:28.640
W-W-Wait. Wait a minute!

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:32.150
B-B-But you have someone that you 
can't forget about, like you said!

00:15:32.150 --> 00:15:33.330
The impregnable—

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.650
That was you.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:35.870
Huh?

00:15:36.570 --> 00:15:40.750
You were always reading books 
on a bench in the park, right?

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:41.890
Oh...

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.290
You are my first love,

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:49.900
the impregnable park
princess. That girl is you.

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:51.400
Huh?

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:52.400
Huh?

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:53.900
Huh?!

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:58.400
Honestly, just how impregnable are you?

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.800
B-B-But that can't be...

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:02.410
I'll be responsible about this.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:07.180
I want to prioritize the feelings you have 
about wanting to do your best at work.

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:12.420
That's why we'll put aside the talk 
of our engagement. For now.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:14.050
But...

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:18.630
I'm not going to give up.

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:22.270
You will come to feel the same 
way about me. I'm sure of it.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.430
So prepare yourself.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:27.430
All right, I managed to say everything!

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.210
Happy to continue working with you.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.540
Yes.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:44.220
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:44.220
Okay, open wide!

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.720
I can feed myself, y'know.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.450
Not a chance. Now, open wide!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.060
Open!

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:00.230
Oh, Tsubameno-san! Listen to this!

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:04.260
Er, um... you're a bit too close.

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:06.150
I had heard the rumors about this, but...

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.240
Not at all! This is normal, right?

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.990
No, y-you're far too close!

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.240
No, no, no.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.240
Yes, yes, yes.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:15.530
Job well done.

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:16.900
Job well done.

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:27.260
It's over, Yasuhiko.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.280
You're writing something again?

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.520
I just want to write now.

00:17:33.390 --> 00:17:37.270
Even if there's only one person 
in the world who'll read it,

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.270
that's more than enough.

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.280
A kingfisher came?

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.790
I wonder if she'd be pleased.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.610
What do you think, Kijitani?

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:05.520
It is turning out nicely, young master.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.800
Don't call me that! Call me "Chef"!

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:09.300
Yes, Chef!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.140
Chef, it's about time.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:13.460
I know.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.300
Splendid job!

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.310
If you train hard enough, 
there's nothing you can't do.

00:18:22.310 --> 00:18:24.900
It's such a superb beef stew.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:26.810
It is pretty good, isn't it?

00:18:27.110 --> 00:18:29.960
I will go fetch Kuze-sama.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:30.820
What?

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:35.680
There is not a girl alive who would 
not fall for you after eating this.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.310
Wait, don't be so hasty!

00:18:37.310 --> 00:18:38.560
You are amazing, youn—

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:40.560
Don't call me "young master"!

00:18:47.720 --> 00:18:50.840
<i>I'm sure she'd enjoy this one.</i>

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:57.580
There's no way I can give up.

00:19:17.890 --> 00:19:21.540
Moritsune-sensei, I'm returning your book.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.080
It's no longer something I should have.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:29.880
I think I'll tell her about you one day.

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.630
It's been a while, hasn't it?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.380
You can have this.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:38.380
<b>Indulgence Mirage Rhythm 
Kurando Otonushi</b>

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:39.780
Are you sure? Thank you.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.080
Is that a medical book?

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:44.320
The Psychological Power 
the Mind Exerts on the Body

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.920
Yes, I'm studying hard.

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:49.630
I'd like to open my father's 
clinic again someday.

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:55.400
I aspired to go into medicine because 
I wanted to be like my father.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.880
I'm glad.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:20:01.140
I hope you'll be by my side 
when that time comes.

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:02.640
See you later.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:05.640
Okay, see you...

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:11.360
This will finish it, Kuina-san.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.970
Hey!

00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:20.220
Oh, nice one.

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:22.820
You can't do that, Perry!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:51.600
Forgive me if this is forward, but I have 
prepared some pancakes for you all.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.960
I helped a bit, as well.

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:57.880
So these are Ouchi-san's pancakes, 
the ones I've dreamed about!

00:20:57.880 --> 00:20:59.480
They have a nice color.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.200
And they smell amazing.

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:05.560
Migiwa-sensei, Gramps' pancakes 
are the best in the world.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:08.530
I'm looking forward to trying them.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:13.320
This gloss, this shine...
It's almost like a work of art.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:16.140
Now, let's dig in before they get cold.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:18.210
Then...

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.110
Let's eat!

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:30.710
Bewitching Tales of the Imperial Capital

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.710
-Nil Admirari-

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:38.170
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:41.960
<i>The story of the girl's fluctuating fate,</i>

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:47.560
<i>which began with the tragedy that befell 
her brother, has now come to an end.</i>

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:52.270
<i>But that is the beginning 
of another new story.</i>

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:59.600
<i>Fate and stories are tied to the future.</i>

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.650
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her tomorrow.</i>

00:23:17.140 --> 00:23:18.440
Please spare me!

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:21.360
Seriously, you again?

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:23.090
How many times does this make now?

00:23:24.050 --> 00:23:25.650
You're the ones from before!

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:27.770
You should really remember who we are by now.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:29.730
Kuze, will you do the honors?

00:23:30.200 --> 00:23:31.110
Okay.

00:23:32.870 --> 00:23:35.680
We're the Imperial Library Intelligence 
Asset Management Bureau.
